      "vision_reason": "This is an archaeological stone sculpture head wearing a pointed cap, explicitly titled a \"Central Asian Figure\" — a headwear type associated with ancient Scythian/Central Asian peoples, not a garment or ethnic marker of the Persian (Iranian) people specifically, and it depicts a foreign type rather than something made/worn by Persians themselves. However, it was found/held in Iran and such pointed-cap figures do appear in Achaemenid-era art of the Iranian plateau, so a headwear plausibly worn within ancient Iranian culture is defensible.",
